# jemdoc: menu{MENU}{using.html}
= jemdocx -- running jemdoc

jemdocx requires Python 3.8 or newer and has no third-party Python runtime
dependencies. From the repository root, process a source file with:

~~~
{}{sh}
python3 jemdoc index.jemdoc
~~~

On Windows, use +py -3 jemdoc index.jemdoc+. The command creates +index.html+.
The +.jemdoc+ extension can be omitted.

== Output and configuration
Choose an output file with +-o+:

~~~
{}{sh}
python3 jemdoc -o html/index.html index.jemdoc
~~~

Load a custom HTML configuration with +-c+:

~~~
{}{sh}
python3 jemdoc -c site.conf -o html/index.html index.jemdoc
~~~

The default output references +jemdoc.css+. Copy +css/jemdoc.css+ from the
repository next to the generated HTML, or supply your own stylesheet through a
configuration or modeline.

== Equation backend
MathJax 4 is the default and requires no local TeX installation:

~~~
{}{sh}
python3 jemdoc --math mathjax index.jemdoc
~~~

Use +--math png+ for classic +latex+ and +dvipng+ images, or +--math none+ to
leave equation markup untouched.

== Other commands
- +python3 jemdoc --help+ prints the command-line overview.
- +python3 jemdoc --version+ prints version and optional PNG-tool information.
- +python3 jemdoc --show-config+ prints the default HTML configuration.

See [htmlchanges.html HTML configuration], [modelines.html modelines], and
[menu.html menus] for site-level customization.
